Z||000002||mrfixit58||01-26-2001||10:45 AM||||Hummm... How are you going to regulate the temperature? You may want to build a shield in front of the burners to prevent a hot spot from developing on the painted piece's side facing that direction. Great size. If you can work out a few bugs, it'll be great!<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||01-26-2001||11:49 AM||||Roy, the LP burners have 6 heat settings<BR>8,000 - 24,000 BTU's<P>Elect. commercial oven burners (2) 0 - 500 deg. each. I also have a Raytek IR thermometer that reads 25 - 750 deg.<P>That should take care of it???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DXR_DAD<P>PS. Shields?..........ok. Thanks<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 01-26-2001).]||||reg||5
