Z||000005||DXR_DAD||01-26-2001||04:22 PM||||Hot Coat said use elect. oven not gas?? but did not say anything about LP ?? that's why I also added the elect. burners. I'm sure that I'll find a way to make it work! Will also bake painted parts and heat metal  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The biggest part is done. I can always add to the  cabinet whatever I need.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks Guys! I'll be lettin ya know how it works and what works best.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000006||mrfixit58||01-26-2001||04:52 PM||||DAD,<P>I mentioned shields because it looks like the burners are sticking directly through the back of the cabinet (i.e., the flame will be visible on the back wall). My thought of the shield was to difuse the heat a little to prevent the side (of the piece you've painted) closest to the flame from curing too quickly and maybe causing problems. <P>Also, is there any insulation on the cabinet? It didn't look like it. You may be able to use less gas or electricity and get a better "even" heat if you were to wrap it with some flame proof insulation.<P>I'm not trying to be critical, just throwing out some ideas that may help if you run into some problems. Besides... I like your style!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Good luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||14
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||01-26-2001||05:18 PM||||Thanks Roy, All info will help!!<BR>Steve, (aka DaRkLoRD) mentioned Fire Bricks?<BR>just for that, lined on the inside.<P>I did fire it up, the flames were not that big,  but?...  the little silver shield on the burners may do it, if not thanks alot for the tip||||reg||1
