Z||000017||Bruce||01-27-2001||08:05 PM||||Is powder coating for cosmetic purposes or does it help with minimizing heat, say, in the V6 manifolds? Anyone had the manifolds jet-coated? What's the price.<BR>End of questions.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Cooter||01-27-2001||08:33 PM||||I used some Tech-Line thermal barrier on my kart's piston and on the inside/outside of the header. I also monster wrapped the header with the insulator wrap. The coatings held up well and the wrapped header kept me from burning my arm while adjusting the carb. I will eventually get some of the exhaust on my 3.4 coated for heat management and for appearance- there are several colors of the coatings to choose from- even "metallic" colors.||||reg||1
Z||000019||hugh||01-27-2001||08:47 PM||||Propane is a damp heat,as is any flame source that uses the oxygen from the air.The moisture in the air condenses on the part being heated,because of the temperature difference between the flame and the part until it gets above the dew point of the flame.||||reg||1
